    p=['A trust is created when a person (the author or settlor) transfers property to trustees to be held for the benefit of others. **Private trusts** are governed by the Indian Trusts Act, 1882, while **public charitable trusts** are governed by state laws or general principles, and are registered by executing a trust deed before the sub-registrar.',
       'Trusts are a simple, popular structure for charitable, educational and religious work. Once registered, a charitable trust can apply for 12A and 80G registration under the Income Tax Act.'],
    b=[('Simple to form', 'A trust deed, trustees and registration are all you need.'),
       ('Tax exemption', 'Eligible to apply for 12A and 80G.'),
       ('Low compliance', 'No MCA filings. Income tax returns and audit when required.'),
       ('Control by trustees', 'The deed sets out how trustees are appointed and replaced.')],
    inc=['Drafting the trust deed', 'Guidance on stamp duty and registration', 'Appointment at the sub-registrar office', 'Trust PAN application', 'Bank account guidance', '12A and 80G guidance'],
    g='Stamp duty on the trust deed and registration charges vary by state.',
    d=[('Settlor and trustee KYC', 'PAN, Aadhaar and photographs.'), ('Registered office proof', 'Utility bill and NOC from the owner.'), ('Trust objects', 'A short description of what the trust will do.'), ('Initial corpus', 'Amount or property being settled into the trust.'), ('Two witnesses', 'With identity proof, for registration.')],
    s=[('Plan the trust', 'We understand your objects and suggest trustee and governance clauses.'),
       ('Draft the deed', 'The trust deed is drafted for your review.'),
       ('Registration', 'The deed is signed and registered before the sub-registrar.'),
       ('PAN and tax setup', 'We apply for the trust\'s PAN and guide you on 12A and 80G.')],
    f=[('How many trustees does a trust need?', 'Law does not fix a minimum for public trusts, but at least two trustees are usual. The deed can set a range.'),
       ('Is a trust better than a Section 8 company?', 'A trust is quicker and cheaper with less compliance. A Section 8 company has stronger governance and is often preferred by CSR donors.'),
       ('Can a trust own property?', 'Trust property is held in the names of the trustees for the trust\'s purposes.'),
       ('Do I need to file returns?', 'Yes. A trust must file income tax returns, and audit applies once income crosses the threshold for charitable entities.')],
